'''timber<sup>2</sup>†''' (tim′bėr), ''n.'' [Also ''timbre, timmer;'' < F. ''timbre'' = LG. ''timmer'' = MHG. ''zimber'', G. ''zimmer'' = Sw. ''timmer'' = Dan. ''simmer'' (< G.), a bundle of skins; origin unknown. It has been conjectured to be a particular use of LG. ''timmer'', etc., a room, hence 'a roomful,' a given number, 40 or 120 according to the animals signified: see ''timber''<sup>1</sup>.] A certain number or tale of skins, being forty of marten, ermine, sable, and the like, and one hundred and twenty of others.

